    "body": "Fixes #776.\n\n## Problem\n\n`int_to_state(state, bracket_notation=False)` is ambiguous and non-invertible for `sps > 10`. The non-bracket branch builds a fixed-width **decimal** field string and strips the spaces, so multi-digit occupations merge into an unparseable run of digits:\n\n```python\nboson_basis_1d(L=4, Nb=10).int_to_state(states[0], False)  # -> '10000'  (should encode |10,0,0,0>)\n```\n\n`'10000'` is indistinguishable from a length-5 state, is non-injective within a sector (`(11,0,0,0)` and `(1,10,0,0)` both → `'11000'` at `sps=12`), and does not round-trip through `state_to_int()` / `index()`, which parse via `int(s, sps)` (base-`sps`).\n\nAdditionally, `basis_1d._index` calls `int(s)` before the `type(s) is str` check, so a base-`sps` string with letter digits (`'A000'`) raises before reaching the string branch.\n\n## Fix\n\n- `basis_1d` and `basis_general` `_int_to_state`: emit `np.base_repr(state, sps).zfill(N)` for the non-bracket form — a true base-`sps` digit string, the exact inverse of `int(s, sps)`. Raise a clear error for `sps > 36` (beyond the base-36 alphabet).\n- `basis_1d._index`: check the `str` case first so letter-digit Fock strings parse correctly.\n- Bracket notation (`bracket_notation=True`) is unchanged.\n\n## Compatibility\n\nFor `sps <= 10` (the overwhelmingly common case) the output is **byte-for-byte identical** to before (`'2000'`, `'110'`, …). Only `sps > 10` behaviour changes — from broken to correct.\n\n| occupation | before (`sps=11`) | after |\n|---|---|---|\n| `[10,0,0,0]` | `'10000'` (ambiguous) | `'A000'` |\n| `[9,1,0,0]`  | `'9100'`             | `'9100'` |\n\n## Tests\n\n`test/test_int_to_state_multidigit.py` covers round-trip via `state_to_int()`/`index()`, injectivity, the previously-colliding pair, `basis_general`, and that `sps <= 10` is unchanged. The three `sps > 10` tests fail on `master` and pass with this change.\n\n---\n> Draft: opened for maintainer review. Happy to adjust the chosen representation (e.g. behaviour for `sps > 36`, or a separator-based scheme) to match project preferences.\n",
