    "body": "**quspin:** 1.0.1 | **Platform:** macOS (ARM + Intel) | **Python:** 3.12\n\n### Problem\n\n`import quspin` raises a hard `ImportError` on macOS after upgrading to 1.0.1:\n\n```\nImportError: dlopen(...hcp_basis.cpython-312-darwin.so, 0x0002):\n  Library not loaded: /opt/homebrew/opt/libomp/lib/libomp.dylib\n  Reason: tried: '/opt/homebrew/opt/libomp/lib/libomp.dylib' (no such file)\n```\n\n1.0.1 is the first release to declare `quspin-extensions` as a hard dependency. The 0.1.8 macOS wheels hardcode an rpath to Homebrew's `libomp` but don't bundle it — so any machine without a prior `brew install libomp` breaks on import.\n\n### Workaround\n\n```bash\nbrew install libomp\n```\n\n### Fix\n\nA fix is open on the `quspin-extensions` side: QuSpin/QuSpin-Extensions#38",
    "closed_by": {
      "login": "sourav-condmat",
      "id": 131288311,
      "node_id": "U_kgDOB9NM9w",
